  "finalText": "I fixed the issue the verifier found: T-1070 is assigned to Ines Kovac (E-201) again, and the escalation to Ola Berg (E-402) still stands.\n\n- **What was wrong:** Escalating the ticket had also made Ola the assignee as a side effect. Ola is only on the incident-command rotation, but payroll belongs to business-apps, and the rules say a ticket can't be handed to someone outside the rotation that owns it. I had noticed this before and wrongly left it in place.\n- **Fix:** I checked that Ines is on call for business-apps at the 2026-03-17 19:40 UTC deadline (her shift is 08:00–20:00 UTC), then made her the assignee again. Ola remains the escalation contact, and the status is still \"escalated\".\n- **Handoff note:** I added a correction comment on T-1070. It says Ines is the assignee and Ola is the escalation contact, and tells the next shift to ignore the earlier line saying the escalation made Ola the assignee.\n\nNothing else changed. T-1070 is still sev1 with the 19:40 UTC deadline, and it stays open until T-1071 (payroll reporting replica lag) is closed and the March batch has been rerun and posted. I didn't touch any other tickets.",
